WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.435
-Ricky, now you're known for
having strong opinions

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.636
about all different
kinds of things.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.937
So with that in mind,
I want to play a game

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:07.740
of "Wheel of Opinions!"

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.177
-♪ Wheel of opinions ♪

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:14.247
-There you go.
-[ Laughs ] I love that.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.482
Got a theme tune.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.550
A lot of thought has gone
into the game.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.152
-Here's how it works.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:22.388
I'm gonna hit this button here,
which is bluetooth

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:23.956
attached to the studio,

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:27.393
and it's going to activate
the opinion topic generator.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.162
And it's going to land
on a random topic.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.864
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:33.966
-And whatever it is, you have to
give your opinion on it.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.101
You ready for this?

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.270
-Yeah.
-Alright, here we go buddy.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.039 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:43.810 line:0%
Horoscopes.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.678 line:0%
I like horoscopes.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.147 line:0%
-[ Groans ] Ridiculous.

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:49.716 line:0%
-What?
-Nonsense.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:53.419 line:0%
-Why?
-A pseudoscience.

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:57.756 line:0%
How can your horoscope,
how can people born

00:00:57.756 --> 00:01:00.326 line:0%
around the same time have all
the same characteristics?

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:04.030 line:0%
If they were in people's minds,
because they --

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.232 line:0%
First of all, they would make
them flattering, don't they?

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:09.569 line:0%
They say things like oh, Cancer,
you're brave but considerate.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.739 line:0%
You know, Virgo, logical,
hard working.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.807 line:0%
Not one star sign says,

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.910 line:0%
"You've got bad breath
and you're gullible."

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.212 line:0%
You know?

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:23.816 line:0%
Those daily things that are,
you know, predictions,

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.317 line:0%
they're so vague.

00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:28.087 line:0%
It's all things like, "Today you
will seize an opportunity."

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:29.756 line:0%
Well, what does that mean?

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.323 line:0%
They've got
to say something like...

00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:34.727 line:0%
If it said, "Sally Marsden
in Teddington,

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.962 line:0%
your boss is going to fire you
today because he knows

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:38.697 line:0%
it was you that nicked
the petty cash,"

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:39.999 line:0%
then I'd believe them.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:43.936 line:0%
But until then,
it's absolute nonsense.

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:45.572 line:0%
[ Ding ]
-Let's hear another topic.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.705 line:0%
Here we go.

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:48.641 line:0%
[ Beeping ]
-Made up nonsense.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.912 line:0%
-Weed gummies.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.047 line:0%
I don't think
you're a weed gummy guy.

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:58.584 line:0%
-Well, I mean, I think
they're probably good

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:01.487 line:0%
for weaning kids on to drugs.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.656 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.726 line:0%
No!
-If you're like,

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.528 line:0%
"Little Tommy
won't smoke his joint."

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:12.364 line:0%
Give him a weed gummy.
Give him a weed gummy.

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:13.199 line:0%
That will help.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.400 line:0%
[ Laughing ]
[ Ding ]

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.169 line:0%
-Here we go, another topic.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.304 line:0%
[ Beeping ]
We're moving.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.343 line:0%
Alright, mechanical pencils.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:27.680 line:0%
When you click and the lead
comes, you know.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.316 line:0%
-Why?
What was up with the pencil?

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.685 line:0%
What was wrong with the pencil?

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:37.290 line:0%
Who is going these pencils,
they're not good anymore?

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.524 line:0%
What was wrong with it?

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:41.894 line:0%
This invention --
I remember when I worked

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:44.430 line:0%
in an office,
it was a little arm

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.866 line:0%
that went down when
you wanted a paper clip.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:49.001 line:0%
Like, people are going,
"I can't pick up

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:51.503 line:0%
paper clips anymore.

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:52.839 line:0%
Fingers are so passe.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.006 line:0%
I can't pick up paper."

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.741 line:0%
It's been made up.

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:58.244 line:0%
No one needed it.
What was wrong with a pencil?

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.045 line:0%
Although I think that
about a lot of stuff,

00:03:00.045 --> 00:03:01.681 line:0%
like belt buckles now.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.182 line:0%
They're like trying to do
the Rubik's cube.

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:04.183 line:0%
What was up with the belt?

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:07.286 line:0%
And watch straps,
absolute nonsense.

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:08.654 line:0%
It's fine.

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:12.825 line:0%
I got a pair of trainers,
and it was ridiculous.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.361 line:0%
You had to pull open a thing,
then pull them up

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.596 line:0%
and then pull a drawstring.

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.197 line:0%
What was up with laces?

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:20.133 line:0%
A pencil is fine.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:24.470 line:0%
No one's ever -- no one's ever
been disappointed with a pencil.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.206 line:0%
It's never -- it's never
been needed to be changed

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:31.276 line:0%
-Well, imagine having --

00:03:31.276 --> 00:03:33.946 line:0%
Imagine having a pencil that...

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:36.082 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.317 line:0%
-Some pencils have disappointed.
[ Ding ]

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.818 line:0%
Let's just say.
Let's just move on.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.219 line:0%
Here we go, another one.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.321 line:0%
Last one, Ricky,
then I'll leave you alone.

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:43.389 line:0%
Thank you so much for doing
this.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.991 line:0%
Here we go.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.893 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:03:49.828 --> 00:03:51.898 line:0%
This is -- I don't know
if we have time for this.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:55.068 line:0%
Space exploration.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:58.937 line:0%
-Ah, I mean, it depends for who.

00:03:58.937 --> 00:04:01.174 line:0%
I like the idea there's
a space program

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:04.710 line:0%
and I love the feat
that we've been over.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:08.214 line:0%
Satellites and, you know,
Hubble telescope

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:10.183 line:0%
and we put a man on the moon.

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:12.151 line:0%
It's incredible.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.886 line:0%
It makes me laugh as well.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:18.691 line:0%
When you see members of like,
the human race taking credit

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.260 line:0%
for things
that a few people did.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:25.097 line:0%
Like, suddenly these people go,
"We put a man on the moon."

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:26.332 line:0%
I go, what do you mean we?

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.967 line:0%
You live in a [bleep] bin.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:30.536 line:0%
You couldn't even point
to the moon,

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:36.041 line:0%
so stop taking credit for things
the rest of mankind have done.

00:04:36.041 --> 00:04:39.344 line:0%
-You had nothing to do
with the moon landing.

00:04:39.344 --> 00:04:41.246 line:0%
-Yeah, you did nothing

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:46.018 line:0%
And I think it's, you know,
it's great as a science program.

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:49.822 line:0%
They're bringing in this thing
where I was offered

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:53.659 line:0%
on one of these things to go in
space for 15 minutes,

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.895 line:0%
and it was like a group
of like billionaires

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:59.331 line:0%
and they offered me a chance
to be the first comedian

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:02.401 line:0%
to do a stand-up show in space.

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:04.137 line:0%
I went, no.
I'm not going to risk --

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.638 line:0%
That's mad.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.807 line:0%
I'm careful crossing the road.

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:11.110 line:0%
Also, these people that pay
like $300,000

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.978 line:0%
to go in space
and have a look around.

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:15.481 line:0%
They go, here's Ricky Gervais
doing 10 minutes.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:19.151 line:0%
they can watch me on YouTube
and now they've blown $300,000.

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:21.253 line:0%
Look out the window.
That's the other thing.

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:23.055 line:0%
People say let's go into space,
and you look up.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:24.389 line:0%
We're in space.

00:05:24.389 --> 00:05:26.592 line:0%
We're in space now.
We're right in the middle.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.961 line:0%
There's nothing you can see
that you can't see from here.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:30.730 line:0%
It's like me getting out
of the chair and going over

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.398 line:0%
there and going,
I can see the chair from here.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:35.401 line:0%
You were in the chair.
You were in the chair.

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.636 line:0%
There's nothing.
You're not going to find --

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:39.071 line:0%
Well, we might find
a new planet.

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:40.573 line:0%
Where is this planet?

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.841 line:0%
It'll take you about 1,000 years
to get there.

00:05:42.841 --> 00:05:45.778 line:0%
What do they expect a find when
they freeze and they go there?

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:48.815 line:0%
They expect to find this
an amazing race of things

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:50.749 line:0%
that tells us all
the secrets of the universe

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:52.918 line:0%
and it'll be big slug at that.

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:55.688 line:0%
And you'll get there
and it's like -- You go,

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:58.424 line:0%
Oh, is there -- how can we cure
everything?

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.926 line:0%
And they go, "I don't know.

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:03.763 line:0%
We're space --
we're space slugs.

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:06.032 line:0%
We're absolute -- we're moronic.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.733 line:0%
So it won't be
what people think.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.135 line:0%
It will never be as good
as people think.

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:13.873 line:0%
So just stay at home and watch
Netflix, "After Life."

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:16.475 line:0%
-We're in -- we're in space.

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:18.511 line:0%
-Yeah, we're right in the
[bleep] middle of it.

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:19.879 line:0%
[ Ding ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.114 line:0%
That's all the time we have
for "Wheel of Opinions!"

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:24.150 line:0%
My thanks again
to Ricky Gervais.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.919 line:0%
You can watch his show
"After Life" on Netflix.

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:28.254 line:0%
Oh, my gosh.

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:30.022 line:0%
My face hurts yet again.
You've done it.

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:31.457 line:0%
Ricky, thanks so much
for being here.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:32.425 line:0%
I needed a laugh.

